{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"affable-soulless-gosling","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Reported by, not investigated by, an adjacent session\n\nSurfaced while confirming the fix for bug 8070 (external-integration canary). Per operator\ninstruction this was NOT investigated — epic e369 is actively held by another session and owns this\nsubject matter. Filing it here so the owning session sees it. **The root cause below is a candidate,\nnot a finding.**\n\n## Observed (live CI, reproducible)\n\nRun 30651750699 — `workflow_dispatch` of `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml` on `main` at\ncommit `b7e6ac963`, 2026-07-31. Job **\"jira DC harness smoke (real Jira Data Center, ephemeral)\"**:\n\n```\ntests/external/live_jira_dc/test_reconcile_pass.py:319\nAssertionError: no local ticket was created from DC issue RBJNAZV-1;\n  stdout='invariants: scanned=1 filed=0 (cap=5)\\nOK: applied 1 of 1 mutations\\n'\nassert []\nFAILED test_reconcile_pass.py::test_a_dc_created_ticket_carries_the_shared_jira_provenance\n```\n\nThe failing test is `test_a_dc_created_ticket_carries_the_shared_jira_provenance`.\n\n## Why this is newly visible\n\nThis failure was previously MASKED. Until `b7e6ac963` the whole external tier died at\n`SnapshotRefError` on an unborn `HEAD` before reaching any behaviour under test (bug 8070). With\nsnapshot resolution fixed, the tier now reaches its subject and this assertion fails on its merits.\nSo this is very likely a pre-existing defect that the canary could not previously report, not a new\nregression from `b7e6ac963` — which touched only `tests/external/conftest.py` (adds an empty root\ncommit) and added a unit test.\n\n## Candidate cause — UNCONFIRMED, do not treat as diagnosed\n\n`scanned=1 filed=0` says the inbound record was seen and then not filed. That shape is consistent\nwith OPEN bug **5f48-244c-7063-42d0** — \"DC inbound identity mint fails silently: 'jira-datacenter'\nis not a valid creation_channel\" — where a silent mint failure would drop the record between scan\nand file. Linked `relates_to`. If that is the cause, this ticket is a duplicate and should be closed\nas such rather than worked separately.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The mechanism behind `scanned=1 filed=0` is identified and cited (`path:line`), and it is\n      determined whether this is the same defect as 5f48 (close as duplicate) or distinct.\n- [ ] `test_a_dc_created_ticket_carries_the_shared_jira_provenance` passes against the live DC\n      harness, or the failure is guarded by a credential-free test in the default suite.","id":"0059-c7f0-cce1-4077","parent_id":"e369-a449-4773-48fb","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"DC inbound filing is a no-op in live CI: reconcile reports scanned=1 filed=0, no local ticket created from DC issue"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785520786072205001,"uuid":"5aad06f0-4a4f-4c5a-981f-c71f0fca2321"}